# ============================================================================
# 06_ Build ASPC and fibroblast-stroma signatures — v9 ADAPTIVE HIERARCHY
# ============================================================================
#
# SELECTION HIERARCHY
#   DOWN/FIBROBLAST:
#     full evidence matrix -> adaptive tier gates -> evidence_score ranking ->
#     top up to cfg$target_size.
#
#   UP/ASPC:
#     full evidence matrix -> exclude selected fibroblast genes -> adaptive tier
#     gates -> augmented pool with optional mandatory AR rescue ->
#     evidence_score ranking -> AR + best N-1 non-AR when rescue is needed.
#
# ADAPTIVE GATES
#   - Tiered thresholds over branch-specific tau, target ratio, and score.
#   - Directional correlation gates are tier-controlled.
#   - Finite tau/ratio/score are always required.
#   - AR rescue never fabricates scores and never overrides fibroblast-first
#     exclusion conflicts.
#
# WHAT IS RETAINED
#   - Existing evidence/annotation channels and weights.
#   - Existing candidate-pool construction and recurrence logic.
#   - Existing bulk correlation calculations and output resources.
#   - Existing unweighted mean z-score bulk signature scoring.
# ============================================================================

